Problem: Solve the following expression and give your answer as a fraction.
$
\dfrac{5}{8} \times 0.5 \times -0.75 = {?}
$
Solution: First get all of the numbers as simplified fractions.
$\qquad
0.5 = \dfrac{5}{10}
= \dfrac{1}{2}
$
