[Problem: Express the fraction as a decimal. $\dfrac{61}{-8}$ ...]
}8\text{ go into }\color{#6495ED}{40}\text{?}$ $\LARGE{0}$ $\LARGE{0}$ $\LARGE{5}$ $\LARGE{4}$ $\LARGE{0}$ $-$ $\LARGE{0}$ $\blue{40}\div8=\green{5}\text{ with a remainder of }\pink{0}$ $\text{The remainder is 0, so we have our answer.}$ $\begin{eqnarray}
\dfrac{61}{-8}
&=& -1 \times (61 \div 8) \\
&=& -1 \times 7.625 \\
&=& -7.625
\end{eqnarray}
$
Answer: -7.625

Problem: Express $0.\overline{5}$ as a common fraction.
Solution: Let $x=0.\overline{5}=0.5\overline{5}$. Then $10x=5.\overline{5}$, and so $10x-x=9x=5\implies x=\boxed{\frac{5}{9}}$.
Answer: \frac{5}{9}

Problem: Express $0.\overline{5}$ as a common fraction in lowest terms.
Solution: Let $x = 0.\overline{5}$. We then have $$ 10x - x = 5.\overline{5} - 0.\overline{5} = 5 \ \ \Rightarrow \ \ x = \boxed{\dfrac{5}{9}}. $$
Answer: \dfrac{5}{9}
